# OBJECT SYMBOL reason   (docs/B5_DESIGN.md 4.1; checked by globals.sh)
# Checker and frontend: nothing a check writes except through once-init or atomics.
c/csymidx serial_counter  atomic
diag cfg_gen_next  atomic
lex cls  once-init (tables_once)
lex cls_dollar  once-init (tables_once)
lex tables_once  once-init flag
srcmgr ps  once-init (ps_once): the page size
srcmgr ps_once  once-init flag
srcmgr lines_lock  a lock
# Fault injection (CEREAL_FAULT), tests only.
thread fault_site  fault injection
thread fault_at  fault injection
thread fault_once  fault injection
thread fault_count  fault injection
# CLI state, set before any thread starts.
fixmode sort_pass  qsort comparator state of cereal fix, single-threaded
main made  CLI state set before threads
main pool  CLI state set before threads
main buf  CLI state set before threads
main fe_opts  CLI options, read-only once units run
main carry_old  CLI state set before threads
main carry_at  CLI state set before threads
main parse_cells  CLI option
main dump_symbols  CLI option
main verify_symbols  CLI option
main rsp  CLI state set before threads (@file arguments)
# Language server: state outside the checker; B5 does not change its thread discipline.
lsp/features tok_cache  server (semantic token cache)
lsp/features tok_next_id  server
lsp/rpc out_fp  server (protocol output)
lsp/rpc out_m  server (its lock)
lsp/server S  the server
lsp/server on  server (once flag)
lsp/project P  the project index scheduler (one per server; the scheduler thread owns it, the mailbox fields are under P.m)
